WEB SOURCE (the specification)
  web/src/components/layout/sidebar/NotionSidebar.tsx — a presentational Notion-style nav tree fed an already
  visibility-filtered tree + three badge counts by its parent (Layout). Its data contract is re-exported from
  LinearSidebar.tsx (LinearSidebarSectionInput / LinearSidebarProps). Regions:
    <nav aria-label="Sidebar navigation">
      → Favorites group (shown when pinnedItems > 0): GroupLabel "Favorites" + pinned NotionRow leaves, each
        with an unpin (×) hover action; rows are inline-filter-narrowed.
      → Pages group: GroupLabel "Pages" + per-section NotionSectionRow (caret + first-item glyph + title +
        filtered count, whole row toggles, caret rotates) + indented (ps-7) NotionRow leaves with a trailing
        badge and a pin (★) / unpin (×) hover action keyed on whether the row is already pinned.
      → Trailing badges (trailingFor): /notifications/alerts → 6px NotificationDot; /vehicles → CountChip
        (n, "99+" cap); /data-repair → CountChip.
      → Empty-filter branch (role=status): "No matches." + a "Clear filter" reset, when the inline tree filter
        (filterTokens > 0) leaves zero expanded sections.
    Interactive state held in component useState: the per-section collapse set (all collapsed EXCEPT the
    active section; the active section auto-expands when it changes) and the inline tree-filter text.
  Data sources: useTranslation + useLocation. No data hooks — the parent computes + feeds the tree; the leaf's
  own variation is the favorites visibility, the per-section caret/collapse, the count>0 section filter, the
  trailing badges, and the empty-filter render.
  i18n keys extracted: nav.sidebar, nav.favorites, nav.pages, nav.filterNoMatch, nav.filterClear, plus the
  dynamic nav.vehicleCount / nav.staleCount (CountChip aria) and nav.pinPage / nav.unpinPage (action aria).

